  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>The Tikayan Le Méditerranée campsite sits at the tip of the Giens peninsula, in Hyères, 150 m from La Badine beach according to the official website. It offers only mobile homes for rent (101, for 2 to 8 people, air-conditioned) and no pitches for tents, caravans or motorhomes. On site: a restaurant-pizzeria and a grocery (official website), plus a playground and two petanque courts (Tourisme avec mon chien directory).</p>

      <h2>What to know before you book</h2>
      <p>The official website's FAQ answers: "Yes, dogs under 40 kg are accepted in most of our rentals". The rental pages show a "Dog under 40 kg allowed" pictogram: some rentals do not have it, so check the page of the accommodation you choose.</p>
      <p>Tikayan's page on dog policy sets the rules common to its campsites: dogs under 40 kg, no category 1 or 2 dogs, an up-to-date health record shown on arrival, dogs on a lead in communal areas, no dogs in water areas, and no animal left alone on a mobile home terrace. Mobile homes accept up to 2 dogs, and some sites limit it to one dog per accommodation.</p>
      <p>For the supplement, a tour operator writes €5 per day and per animal, a specialist directory €3 to €6 per day depending on the period; the official pages read give no amount.</p>
      <p><strong>To check before you go:</strong> the amount of the supplement, the number of dogs allowed in the chosen accommodation and whether dogs are accepted in the campsite's restaurant (stated by a directory, not by the official website), by calling the campsite on 04 94 58 21 06.</p>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The La Badine beach restaurants can be reached on foot from the campsite according to the official website (dog rules of these restaurants not checked).</p>

      <h2>Sources</h2>
      <p>Official website tikayan.com (campsite page, FAQ and dog-friendly campsite page) read on 19/11/2026; Tourisme avec mon chien directory and tour operator pages for the supplement, read on 19/11/2026.</p>
